# The source mockups stay out of git.
#
# Six of them come to just under a gigabyte, and git keeps every version of a
# binary for ever — one commit of these would be a permanent tax on every
# clone the repo ever serves. They are bought files that live on this machine
# and in whatever backs it up.
#
# What ships is the flattened JPEG beside each one, which is what the browser
# can use anyway: a 240MB layered document is not something a canvas opens.
# Remaking one after editing the PSD:
#
#   sips -s format png --resampleWidth 1400 <file>.psd --out /tmp/t.png
#   magick /tmp/t.png -quality 84 src/templates/<name>.jpg
#
# Then re-measure its `area` in templates.ts, because a re-export can move the
# subject by a few pixels and the placement is in fractions of the image.
*.psd
